# Agent-tooling local config — NEVER commit. .codex/config.toml holds live
# secrets (Supabase service_role JWT, DB password, Railway + GitHub tokens);
# AGENTS.md is local agent scratch. Repo is PUBLIC — a stray `git add .`
# must not publish these. (Added 2026-06-08, launch-readiness audit.)
/.codex/
/AGENTS.md

# Backup tarballs (the documented `edu-cms-backup-*.tar.gz` procedure writes
# these to repo root) + private keys/certs — never commit to a public repo.
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
edu-cms-backup-*
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.crt
# ...with ONE deliberate exception: Supabase's PUBLIC root CA. It is a trust
# ANCHOR, not a secret — the same bytes every Supabase customer downloads, and
# the same root the server already hands to any client that connects. Pinning
# it in git is what makes `sslaccept=strict` (database TLS identity
# verification) possible without making every production build depend on a
# third-party S3 URL staying up. Its sha256 is asserted at image build time —
# see the Dockerfile and packages/database/certs/README.md.
!packages/database/certs/supabase-prod-ca-2021.crt
